  "id": "BIT-golang-2026-56857",
  "summary": "Root.Mkdir(All) can follow junctions out of the root on Windows in os",
  "details": "On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).",
